    "question": "Judy Naden, CFA, is an analyst covering the aerospace sector. Naden's recommendations often impact stock prices within the sector. Naden finalizes an investment recommendation on a company using published financial data and nonmaterial, nonpublic information gathered from industry experts and competitors. She distributes the report only to her firm's clients by email. Her firm's clients trade on this information before her report is made available to the general public a few days later. Has Naden most likely violated the Standards?",
