    "question": "Rebecca Chen, CFA, is a portfolio manager at an investment firm. Chen has been specializing in the technology sector. She recently expanded her coverage to the oil sector. Chen attends training to ensure that she has sufficient knowledge of the oil sector before taking the new role. After comprehensive research, Chen concludes that First Oil Company (FOC) is undervalued and buys FOC shares for her clients for whom the investment is suitable. Two months later, FOC's price declines by 20%. Has Chen violated the Standards?",
